  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "A block of mass m is placed on a smooth inclined wedge $A B C$ of inclination $\\theta$ as shown in the figure. The wedge is given an acceleration 'a' towards the right. The relation between a and $\\theta$ for the block to remain stationary on the wedge is\r\n\r\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/bitsat/6elWAXz6q9osdRlGR5hP02iRBVuwHR0J8DkFfiRalJA.original.fullsize.png\">",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "Mq4B9",
      "text": "$a=\\frac{g}{\\operatorname{cosec} \\theta}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "zhidZ",
      "text": "$a=\\frac{g}{\\sin \\theta}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "KVnWx",
      "text": "$a=g \\tan \\theta$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "Bpv1y",
      "text": "$a=g \\cos \\theta$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Let the mass of block is m. It will remains stationary if forces acting on it are in equilibrium. i.e., $m a \\cos \\theta=m g \\sin \\theta$\r\n\r\n$\\Rightarrow a=g \\tan \\theta$\r\n\r\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/bitsat/6Kt7aR7rSEsAgzZdB-12ihl9_xlN6SnNnJoueun6tjg.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\r\n\r\nHere $\\mathrm{ma}=$ Pseudo force on block,\r\n\r\n$\\mathrm{mg}=$ weight",
    "image": null
  },
